92186384188 13194139536112 true] [17592186384187 1089 "q-40665" 13194139536112 true] [17592186384187 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139536112 true] [17592186384187 1100 "Find a matrix that defines the orthogonal projection of ${R}^{3}$ onto the plane whose parametric equation is $r=sv+tw$, where\n\n$$\nv=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,w=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139536112 true] [17592186384187 1113 #uuid "7c0b3628-a42d-53f5-bbf5-c943da2f8ab1" 13194139536112 true] [17592186384187 1145 "Recall that the matrix ${P}_{S}=A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T}$ maps any vector $x\\in {R}^{n}$ onto its orthogonal projection in the subspace $S$ spanned by the columns of the matrix $A.$ \n\nNotice that the plane $r=sv+tw$ is actually the subspace $\\text{Span}{v,w}.$ \nHence, we have \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{S} & =A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}]{([\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]{[\\begin{aligned}6 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 6\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{35}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}6 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{35}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 & 4 & 13 \\\\ 5 & 11 & -8\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{35}[\\begin{aligned}10 & 15 & 5 \\\\ 15 & 26 & -3 \\\\ 5 & -3 & 34\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536112 true] [17592186384188 1000 #edb/ref 17592186384189 13194139536112 true] [17592186384188 1000 #edb/ref 1759218